(function(E){ const x = E["hr-m3"] = E["hr-m3"] || {units:{}}; x.units["hr-3-3"] = {"explain":{"id":"c-hr-3-3-e","course":"hr","unit":"hr-3-3","type":"explain","level":"B1","title":{"en":"Notes and evaluation","tr":"Notlar ve değerlendirme","fa":"یادداشت‌برداری و ارزیابی"},"objective":{"en":"After this lesson, you can write fair interview notes that report what the candidate said, and a short recommendation.","tr":"Bu dersin sonunda adayın söylediklerini aktaran adil mülakat notları ve kısa bir öneri yazabileceksin.","fa":"بعد از این درس می‌توانی یادداشت‌های منصفانه‌ی مصاحبه بنویسی که حرف متقاضی را نقل می‌کنند و در آخر یک توصیه‌ی کوتاه بدهی."},"hook":{"en":"Write what was said, not what you felt, because the candidate can ask to read your notes. Omar wrote 'a bit lazy maybe'. Leyla wrote what Karim said. Only one of these notes is fair.","tr":"Hissettiğini değil, söyleneni yaz, çünkü aday notlarını okumak isteyebilir. Omar 'biraz tembel galiba' yazdı. Leyla ise Karim'in ne söylediğini yazdı. Bu notlardan yalnızca biri adil.","fa":"چیزی را بنویس که گفته شد، نه حس خودت را، چون متقاضی می‌تواند بخواهد یادداشت‌هایت را بخواند. عمر نوشت «شاید کمی تنبل». لیلا نوشت کریم چه گفت. فقط یکی از این یادداشت‌ها منصفانه است."},"before":{"en":"Rewrite opinion notes on a candidate as fair notes: what they said, one gap and a short recommendation.","tr":"Bir aday hakkındaki görüş notlarını adil notlara çevir: ne söyledi, bir eksik ve kısa bir öneri.","fa":"یادداشت‌های نظری درباره‌ی یک داوطلب را به یادداشت منصفانه تبدیل کن: چه گفت، یک کمبود و یک پیشنهاد کوتاه."},"rounds":[[1,4],[2,3]],"stats":[{"label":{"en":"Key points","tr":"Ana nokta","fa":"نکته‌ی اصلی"},"value":"4"},{"label":{"en":"Key phrases","tr":"Anahtar ifade","fa":"عبارت کلیدی"},"value":"4"},{"label":{"en":"Practice tasks","tr":"Alıştırma","fa":"تمرین"},"value":"5"}],"points":[{"eyebrow":{"en":"The skill","tr":"Beceri","fa":"مهارت"},"head":{"en":"Write what was said, not what you felt","tr":"Hissettiğini değil, söyleneni yaz","fa":"چیزی را بنویس که گفته شد، نه حس خودت را"},"body":{"en":"A word like \"lazy\" can't be checked, and it can hide bias. A fair note says what the person said or did. If something is missing, name the gap calmly.","tr":"\"Tembel\" gibi bir kelime kontrol edilemez ve önyargıyı gizleyebilir. Adil bir not, kişinin ne söylediğini ya da yaptığını yazar. Eksik bir şey varsa bu boşluğu sakince belirt.","fa":"کلمه‌ای مثل «تنبل» را نمی‌شود بررسی کرد و ممکن است پیش‌داوری را پنهان کند. یادداشت منصفانه می‌گوید آن شخص چه گفته یا چه کرده است. اگر چیزی کم است، آرام بگو چه چیزی کم است."}},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The language","tr":"Dil","fa":"زبان"},"head":{"en":"Reporting what candidates said","tr":"Adayların söylediklerini aktarmak","fa":"نقل حرف متقاضی‌ها"},"steps":[{"en":"said + what; told + person + what.","tr":"said + ne söylendiği; told + kişi + ne söylendiği.","fa":"بعد از said خود حرف می‌آید؛ بعد از told اول شخص می‌آید و بعد حرف.","ex":"She said she had led a team. He told us he had driven in Dubai."},{"en":"Move the tense one step back.","tr":"Zamanı bir adım geriye kaydır.","fa":"زمان فعل را یک قدم به عقب ببر.","ex":"'I can start in May' becomes he said he could start in May."},{"en":"Judge with a hedge: appears, seems, limited evidence.","tr":"Değerlendirmeyi yumuşat: appears, seems, limited evidence.","fa":"قضاوت را محتاطانه بگو: appears، seems، ⁨limited evidence⁩.","ex":"There is limited evidence of night-shift experience."}],"table":{"headers":{"en":["Candidate said","Your note"],"tr":["Aday dedi","Senin notun"],"fa":["متقاضی گفت","یادداشت تو"]},"rows":[["\"I led a team of four.\"","She said she had led a team of four."],["\"I can start in May.\"","He told us he could start in May."],["\"I'm working nights now.\"","She said she was working nights."],["(no example given)","There is limited evidence of night-shift experience."]]},"tip":{"en":"Persian be man goft and Turkish bana söyledi put the person with say, so learners write 'said me'. English: said with no person, or told + person.","tr":"Türkçede 'bana söyledi' deriz ve kişi 'söyledi' ile gelir; bu yüzden 'said me' yazılır. İngilizcede said kişi almaz; kişi varsa told kullanılır: He told me...","fa":"در فارسی می‌گوییم «به من گفت»، برای همین فارسی‌زبان‌ها زیاد می‌نویسند «said me». در انگلیسی said شخص نمی‌گیرد؛ اگر شخص هست، told بنویس: «⁨He told me...⁩»"},"wrong":"He said me he had worked nights.","right":"He told me he had worked nights."},{"eyebrow":{"en":"Key phrases","tr":"Anahtar ifadeler","fa":"عبارت‌های کلیدی"},"head":{"en":"Phrases for this task","tr":"Bu görev için ifadeler","fa":"عبارت‌های این کار"},"phrases":[{"phrase":"He told us (that)...","meaning":{"en":"Reports a fact from the interview.","tr":"Mülakattan bir olguyu aktarır.","fa":"یک واقعیت از مصاحبه را گزارش می‌کند."}},{"phrase":"There is limited evidence of...","meaning":{"en":"Names a gap without judging the person.","tr":"Kişiyi yargılamadan bir eksikliği belirtir.","fa":"یک کمبود را می‌گوید، بدون قضاوت درباره‌ی خود شخص."}},{"phrase":"Based on what she said, ...","meaning":{"en":"Links your view to the evidence.","tr":"Görüşünü kanıta bağlar.","fa":"نظر تو را به شواهد گره می‌زند."}},{"phrase":"objective","meaning":{"en":"Based on facts, not feelings.","tr":"nesnel.","fa":"عینی؛ بی‌طرفانه (بر پایه‌ی واقعیت، نه احساس)"}}]},{"eyebrow":{"en":"At work","tr":"İş yerinde","fa":"در محیط کار"},"head":{"en":"Score alone, then discuss","tr":"Önce tek başına puanla, sonra tartış","fa":"اول جداگانه امتیاز بده، بعد بحث کن"},"body":{"en":"Many international companies ask each panel member to score every answer alone before the panel discussion, so the most senior voice does not decide for everyone. In hierarchical workplaces, a junior interviewer may not want to disagree with a manager out loud; written scores first protect their view.","tr":"Birçok uluslararası şirket, heyetteki herkesin her cevabı değerlendirme toplantısından önce tek başına puanlamasını ister; böylece en kıdemli kişinin sesi herkes adına karar vermez. Hiyerarşik işyerlerinde daha az kıdemli bir görüşmeci bir yöneticiye yüksek sesle itiraz etmek istemeyebilir; önce yazılı puan vermek onun görüşünü korur.","fa":"بسیاری از شرکت‌های بین‌المللی از هر عضو هیئت مصاحبه می‌خواهند پیش از جلسه‌ی جمع‌بندی، به هر جواب جداگانه و تنهایی امتیاز بدهد، تا نظر ارشدترین فرد جای نظر همه را نگیرد. در محیط‌های کاری سلسله‌مراتبی، مصاحبه‌گرِ کم‌سابقه‌تر ممکن است نخواهد جلوی مدیر مخالفتش را بلند بگوید؛ امتیازی که از قبل نوشته شده، از نظر او محافظت می‌کند."}}],"example":{"eyebrow":{"en":"Worked example","tr":"Çözümlü örnek","fa":"مثال حل‌شده"},"head":{"en":"From weak to strong","tr":"Zayıftan güçlüye","fa":"از نظر شخصی تا چیزی که گفته شد"},"text":"Facts: He said he had worked in two warehouses. He gave no example of night work.","item":"Seems unreliable. Not sure about him.","why":{"en":"Weak: an opinion, with no evidence. Strong: what he said, and one clear gap.","tr":"Zayıf: kanıtsız bir görüş. Güçlü: söyledikleri ve net bir eksik.","fa":"نسخه‌ی اول یک نظر است، بدون مدرک. نسخه‌ی دوم می‌گوید او چه گفت و دقیقاً چه چیزی کم بود."},"answer":"He said he had worked in two warehouses. There is limited evidence of night work.","cut":["Seems unreliable.","Not sure about him."],"cutHint":{"en":"Tap the feelings that no one can check.","tr":"Kimsenin kontrol edemeyeceği duygulara dokun.","fa":"روی احساساتی بزن که هیچ‌کس نمی‌تواند بسنجدشان."}},"quick":{"prompt":"Why do many panels score each answer alone before they talk?","options":["So the most senior voice does not decide for everyone","So the interview is shorter","So the candidate cannot see the scores"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"So the most senior voice does not decide for everyone: a junior interviewer may not want to disagree out loud, and written scores protect their view.","tr":"Böylece en kıdemli kişinin sesi herkes adına karar vermez: Daha kıdemsiz bir görüşmeci yüksek sesle itiraz etmek istemeyebilir; yazılı puanlar onun görüşünü korur.","fa":"تا صدای ارشدترین آدم برای همه تصمیم نگیرد: مصاحبه‌گر تازه‌کار ممکن است نخواهد بلند مخالفت کند و امتیاز نوشته‌شده از نظرش محافظت می‌کند."},"point":4,"hint2":{"en":"Think about who speaks first on a panel. Whose view could get lost if everyone talks before they score?","tr":"Bir panelde kimin önce konuştuğunu düşün. Herkes puan vermeden önce konuşursa kimin görüşü kaybolabilir?","fa":"فکر کن در جلسه‌ی مصاحبه چه کسی اول حرف می‌زند. اگر همه قبل از امتیاز دادن حرف بزنند، نظر چه کسی ممکن است گم شود؟"}},"remember":{"en":"Could the candidate read your note and say 'Yes, I said that'? Then it is a fair note. Result of this lesson: you can write notes a candidate could read. You also have fair notes in place of a manager's opinions.","tr":"Aday notunu okuyup 'Evet, bunu ben söyledim' diyebilir mi? O zaman adil bir nottur. Bu dersin sonucu: adayın okuyabileceği notlar yazabilirsin ve elinde bir yöneticinin görüşleri yerine adil notlar olur.","fa":"اگر متقاضی یادداشتت را بخواند، می‌تواند بگوید «بله، این را گفتم»؟ پس یادداشت منصفانه است. حالا می‌توانی یادداشت‌هایی بنویسی که متقاضی هم بتواند بخواند. یادداشت‌های منصفانه‌ای هم آماده داری که جای نظرهای مدیر را می‌گیرند."},"b2Point":{"eyebrow":{"en":"B2 track","tr":"B2 yolu","fa":"مسیر B2"},"head":{"en":"Reporting verbs: claim, admit, explain, mention","tr":"Aktarma fiilleri: claim, admit, explain, mention","fa":"فعل‌های نقل قول: claim، admit، explain، mention"},"steps":[{"en":"explain / mention + that + clause; explain TO a person.","tr":"explain / mention + that + cümle; kişiye explain TO.","fa":"بعد از explain و mention کلمه‌ی that و یک جمله می‌آید؛ برای شخص بگو explain to.","ex":"He explained to me that the truck had broken down."},{"en":"admit + -ing.","tr":"admit + -ing.","fa":"بعد از admit فعل -ing‌دار می‌آید.","ex":"She admitted making a mistake with the schedule."},{"en":"claim + to have + past participle: only when you doubt it.","tr":"claim + to have + past participle: yalnızca şüphen varsa.","fa":"بعد از claim شکل to have و اسم مفعول می‌آید؛ فقط وقتی به کارش ببر که به درستی حرف شک داری.","ex":"He claimed to have led the whole project."}],"table":{"headers":{"en":["Verb","Pattern","Example"],"tr":["Fiil","Kalıp","Örnek"],"fa":["فعل","الگو","مثال"]},"rows":[["explain / mention","+ that + clause","He explained that the truck had broken down."],["admit","+ -ing","She admitted making a mistake."],["claim","+ to have + past participle","He claimed to have led the project."]]},"body":{"en":"B2 track: use two different reporting verbs besides said and told in your notes, and choose a neutral verb unless you really doubt the claim.","tr":"B2 yolu: notlarında said ve told dışında iki farklı aktarma fiili kullan; söylenenden gerçekten şüphe etmiyorsan tarafsız bir fiil seç.","fa":"مسیر B2: در یادداشت‌هایت علاوه بر said و told از دو فعل گزارشی دیگر استفاده کن و فعل بی‌طرف را انتخاب کن، مگر اینکه واقعاً به حرف متقاضی شک داشته باشی."}},"source":{"en":"Informed by ICO guidance on recruitment records.","tr":"ICO’nun işe alım kayıtları rehberinden yararlanır.","fa":"با استفاده از راهنمای ICO درباره‌ی سوابق استخدام."}},"grammar":{"id":"c-hr-3-3-g","level":"B1","course":"hr","unit":"hr-3-3","title":"Reporting what candidates said","titleTr":"Adayların söylediklerini aktarmak","exp":{"en":"Interview notes report what the candidate said, not what you felt. Use said with no person after it, or told + a person: \"She said she had led a team of four.\", \"He told us he had driven in Dubai.\" Never \"said me\" and never \"told that\" without a person. In notes, the safe default is to move the tense one step back: \"I led\" becomes \"she said she had led\", \"I can start in May\" becomes \"he said he could start in May\". Then give your evaluation with a hedge: \"There is limited evidence of night-shift experience.\", \"He appears to work well under pressure.\" Hedges show that this is your judgement from the evidence, not a fact about the person. Evidence is uncountable: \"limited evidence\" or \"little evidence\", never \"few evidence\".","tr":"Mülakat notları senin ne hissettiğini değil, adayın ne söylediğini aktarır. Ardından kişi gelmeyen said ya da told + kişi kullan: \"She said she had led a team of four.\", \"He told us he had driven in Dubai.\" Asla \"said me\" deme, kişi olmadan da \"told that\" deme. Notlarda güvenli varsayılan, zamanı bir adım geriye almaktır: \"I led\" → \"she said she had led\", \"I can start in May\" → \"he said he could start in May\". Sonra değerlendirmeni bir yumuşatıcıyla ver: \"There is limited evidence of night-shift experience.\", \"He appears to work well under pressure.\" Bu yumuşatıcılar bunun kişi hakkında bir gerçek değil, kanıta dayalı senin yargın olduğunu gösterir. Evidence sayılamaz: \"limited evidence\" ya da \"little evidence\" denir, asla \"few evidence\" denmez.","fa":"یادداشت مصاحبه باید گزارش کند متقاضی چه گفت، نه اینکه تو چه حسی داشتی. say را بدون مفعول شخصی به کار ببر و tell را همیشه با شخص: «⁨She said she had led a team of four.⁩» و «⁨He told us he had driven in Dubai.⁩» چون در فارسی می‌گوییم «به من گفت»، فارسی‌زبان‌ها زیاد می‌نویسند «said me»؛ این غلط است. «told that» هم بدون شخص غلط است. در یادداشت، امن‌ترین کار این است که زمان فعل را یک پله به عقب ببری: «I led» می‌شود «she said she had led» و «I can start in May» می‌شود «he said he could start in May». بعد ارزیابی‌ات را با زبانی محتاط بنویس: «⁨There is limited evidence of night-shift experience.⁩» یا «⁨He appears to work well under pressure.⁩» این عبارت‌ها نشان می‌دهند این برداشت تو از شواهد است، نه حکمی قطعی درباره‌ی آن آدم. یادت باشد evidence غیرقابل‌شمارش است: «limited evidence» یا «little evidence»، هرگز «few evidence»."},"formsTable":{"headers":{"en":["Candidate said","Your note"],"tr":["Aday dedi","Senin notun"],"fa":["متقاضی گفت","یادداشت تو"]},"rows":[["\"I led a team of four.\"","She said she had led a team of four."],["\"I can start in May.\"","He told us he could start in May."],["\"I'm working nights now.\"","She said she was working nights."],["(no example given)","There is limited evidence of night-shift experience."]]},"wrong":"He said me that he had driven in Dubai.","right":"He told me that he had driven in Dubai.","blank":{"sentence":"She ___ me she had managed cold-chain deliveries.","word":"told","distractors":["said","spoke"]},"wrong2":"There is few evidence of teamwork.","right2":"There is limited evidence of teamwork.","blank2":{"sentence":"There is ___ evidence of night-shift experience.","word":"limited","distractors":["few","many"]},"expParts":{"tryFrom":"blank","hook":{"en":"Omar wrote 'a bit lazy maybe'. Leyla wrote what Karim said. Only one of these notes is fair.","tr":"Omar 'biraz tembel galiba' yazdı. Leyla ise Karim'in ne söylediğini yazdı. Bu notlardan yalnızca biri adil.","fa":"عمر نوشت «شاید کمی تنبل». لیلا نوشت کریم چه گفت. فقط یکی از این یادداشت‌ها منصفانه است."},"tryWhy":{"en":"told: told needs a person after it (told me). said cannot take me directly.","tr":"told: told'dan sonra bir kişi gelir (told me). said doğrudan me alamaz.","fa":"جواب told است: بعد از told یک شخص می‌آید (told me). said نمی‌تواند مستقیم me بگیرد."},"rule":[{"en":"said + what; told + person + what.","tr":"said + ne söylendiği; told + kişi + ne söylendiği.","fa":"بعد از said خود حرف می‌آید؛ بعد از told اول شخص می‌آید و بعد حرف.","ex":"She said she had led a team. He told us he had driven in Dubai."},{"en":"Move the tense one step back.","tr":"Zamanı bir adım geriye kaydır.","fa":"زمان فعل را یک قدم به عقب ببر.","ex":"'I can start in May' becomes he said he could start in May."},{"en":"Judge with a hedge: appears, seems, limited evidence.","tr":"Değerlendirmeyi yumuşat: appears, seems, limited evidence.","fa":"قضاوت را محتاطانه بگو: appears، seems، ⁨limited evidence⁩.","ex":"There is limited evidence of night-shift experience."}],"test":{"en":"Could the candidate read your note and say 'Yes, I said that'? Then it is a fair note.","tr":"Aday notunu okuyup 'Evet, bunu ben söyledim' diyebilir mi? O zaman adil bir nottur.","fa":"اگر متقاضی یادداشتت را بخواند، می‌تواند بگوید «بله، این را گفتم»؟ پس یادداشت منصفانه است."},"contrast":{"en":"Persian be man goft and Turkish bana söyledi put the person with say, so learners write 'said me'. English: said with no person, or told + person.","tr":"Türkçede 'bana söyledi' deriz ve kişi 'söyledi' ile gelir; bu yüzden 'said me' yazılır. İngilizcede said kişi almaz; kişi varsa told kullanılır: He told me...","fa":"در فارسی می‌گوییم «به من گفت»، برای همین فارسی‌زبان‌ها زیاد می‌نویسند «said me». در انگلیسی said شخص نمی‌گیرد؛ اگر شخص هست، told بنویس: «⁨He told me...⁩»"}},"errorWatch":[{"find":["said me","said us","said him","he told that","she told that","they told that"],"fix":{"en":"Use said with no person, or told + person: 'He told me that...' / 'He said that...'","tr":"said'i kişisiz kullan ya da told + kişi: 'He told me that...' / 'He said that...'","fa":"said را بدون شخص بیاور یا told را با شخص: «He told me that...» یا «He said that...»"}},{"find":["few evidence","many evidence","an evidence","evidences","lazy","nice guy"],"fix":{"en":"Evidence is uncountable (limited evidence), and notes need evidence, not labels like 'lazy'.","tr":"Evidence sayılamaz (limited evidence); notlar 'lazy' gibi etiketler değil, kanıt ister.","fa":"evidence شمارش‌پذیر نیست (limited evidence) و یادداشت به شاهد نیاز دارد، نه برچسب‌هایی مثل «lazy»."}}]},"b2":{"id":"c-hr-3-3-b2","level":"B2","track":"B2","course":"hr","unit":"hr-3-3","title":"Reporting verbs: claim, admit, explain, mention","titleTr":"Aktarma fiilleri: claim, admit, explain, mention","exp":{"en":"B2 notes use reporting verbs that show what kind of thing was said, and each verb has its own pattern. Explain that / mention that + clause: \"He explained that the truck had broken down.\" Admit + -ing: \"She admitted making a mistake with the schedule.\" Claim + to have + past participle: \"He claimed to have led the whole project.\" Be careful: claim suggests you are not sure it is true, so in a fair note use it only when you mean that. Neutral choices are said, explained and mentioned. Explain needs to before a person: \"He explained to me that...\", never \"He explained me...\".","tr":"B2 düzeyindeki notlar, ne tür bir şey söylendiğini gösteren aktarma fiilleri kullanır ve her fiilin kendi kalıbı vardır. Explain that / mention that + yan cümle: \"He explained that the truck had broken down.\" Admit + -ing: \"She admitted making a mistake with the schedule.\" Claim + to have + past participle: \"He claimed to have led the whole project.\" Dikkat: claim, söylenenin doğru olduğundan emin olmadığını ima eder; adil bir notta onu ancak bunu kastediyorsan kullan. Tarafsız seçenekler said, explained ve mentioned. Explain fiilinden sonra kişi gelirse to gerekir: \"He explained to me that...\", asla \"He explained me...\" değil.","fa":"در سطح ⁨B2⁩ از فعل‌های گزارشی‌ای استفاده می‌شود که نشان می‌دهند حرف از چه نوعی بوده است، و هر کدام الگوی خودش را دارد. ⁨explain that⁩ یا ⁨mention that⁩ + جمله: «⁨He explained that the truck had broken down.⁩» ⁨admit⁩ + ⁨-ing⁩: «⁨She admitted making a mistake with the schedule.⁩» ⁨claim + to have⁩ + اسم مفعول: «⁨He claimed to have led the whole project.⁩» حواست باشد: ⁨claim⁩ یعنی «ادعا کرد» و نشان می‌دهد تو مطمئن نیستی حرفش درست است؛ پس در یادداشت منصفانه فقط وقتی از آن استفاده کن که واقعاً همین منظور را داری. فعل‌های بی‌طرف ⁨said⁩، ⁨explained⁩ و ⁨mentioned⁩ هستند. یک تله‌ی آشنا برای فارسی‌زبان‌ها: چون می‌گوییم «به من توضیح داد»، می‌نویسند «⁨He explained me⁩». درستش این است: «⁨He explained to me that...⁩»."},"formsTable":{"headers":{"en":["Verb","Pattern","Example"],"tr":["Fiil","Kalıp","Örnek"],"fa":["فعل","الگو","مثال"]},"rows":[["explain / mention","+ that + clause","He explained that the truck had broken down."],["admit","+ -ing","She admitted making a mistake."],["claim","+ to have + past participle","He claimed to have led the project."]]},"wrong":"She admitted to make a mistake with the schedule.","right":"She admitted making a mistake with the schedule.","blank":{"sentence":"He ___ to have led the whole project.","word":"claimed","distractors":["admitted","said"]},"wrong2":"He explained me that the truck had broken down.","right2":"He explained to me that the truck had broken down.","blank2":{"sentence":"She admitted ___ a mistake with the schedule.","word":"making","distractors":["to make","make"]},"useIn":{"en":"B2 track: use two different reporting verbs besides said and told in your notes, and choose a neutral verb unless you really doubt the claim.","tr":"B2 yolu: notlarında said ve told dışında iki farklı aktarma fiili kullan; söylenenden gerçekten şüphe etmiyorsan tarafsız bir fiil seç.","fa":"مسیر B2: در یادداشت‌هایت علاوه بر said و told از دو فعل گزارشی دیگر استفاده کن و فعل بی‌طرف را انتخاب کن، مگر اینکه واقعاً به حرف متقاضی شک داشته باشی."},"exitItem":{"from":"hr-3-3","kind":"blank","prompt":"He mentioned ___ a forklift licence.","options":["to have","having","have"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"having: 'mention' takes -ing. 'To have' and 'have' don't follow mentioned.","tr":"having: 'mention' -ing alır. 'To have' ve 'have' mentioned'dan sonra gelmez.","fa":"having درست است، چون بعد از mention فعل ing‌دار می‌آید. to have و have بعد از mentioned نمی‌آیند."}},"expParts":{"hook":{"en":"Said, explained, admitted, claimed: each verb tells Omar how Leyla heard it.","tr":"Said, explained, admitted, claimed: her fiil Omar'a Leyla'nın bunu nasıl duyduğunu anlatır.","fa":"said، explained، admitted، claimed: هر کدام به عمر می‌گوید لیلا آن حرف را چطور شنیده است."},"tryWhy":{"en":"making: admit is followed by -ing, not to + verb.","tr":"making: admit'ten sonra -ing gelir, to + fiil değil.","fa":"جواب making است: بعد از admit فعل -ing‌دار می‌آید، نه to و فعل."},"rule":[{"en":"explain / mention + that + clause; explain TO a person.","tr":"explain / mention + that + cümle; kişiye explain TO.","fa":"بعد از explain و mention کلمه‌ی that و یک جمله می‌آید؛ برای شخص بگو explain to.","ex":"He explained to me that the truck had broken down."},{"en":"admit + -ing.","tr":"admit + -ing.","fa":"بعد از admit فعل -ing‌دار می‌آید.","ex":"She admitted making a mistake with the schedule."},{"en":"claim + to have + past participle: only when you doubt it.","tr":"claim + to have + past participle: yalnızca şüphen varsa.","fa":"بعد از claim شکل to have و اسم مفعول می‌آید؛ فقط وقتی به کارش ببر که به درستی حرف شک داری.","ex":"He claimed to have led the whole project."}],"test":{"en":"Would you sign this verb in front of the candidate? If 'claimed' sounds like doubt you cannot prove, use 'said'.","tr":"Bu fiili adayın önünde imzalar mıydın? 'claimed' kanıtlayamadığın bir şüphe gibi duruyorsa 'said' kullan.","fa":"حاضری این فعل را جلوی خود متقاضی امضا کنی؟ اگر «claimed» شکی را نشان می‌دهد که نمی‌توانی ثابتش کنی، بنویس «said»."},"contrast":{"en":"Persian be man tozih dad and Turkish bana açıkladı lead to 'explained me'. English explain needs to before the person.","tr":"Türkçedeki 'bana açıkladı' yapısı 'explained me' hatasına yol açar. İngilizcede kişiden önce to gerekir: explained to me.","fa":"«به من توضیح داد» در فارسی باعث می‌شود بنویسیم «explained me». در انگلیسی پیش از شخص to لازم است: «explained to me»."}},"errorWatch":[{"find":["explained me","explained us","explained him","admitted to make","admitted make"],"fix":{"en":"explain to + person; admit + -ing: 'He explained to me that...', 'She admitted making a mistake.'","tr":"explain to + kişi; admit + -ing: 'He explained to me that...', 'She admitted making a mistake.'","fa":"بعد از explain، اول to و بعد شخص می‌آید؛ بعد از admit فعل -ing‌دار: «He explained to me that...» و «She admitted making a mistake.»"}}]},"vocab":{"id":"c-hr-3-3-v","level":"B1","category":"vocab","course":"hr","unit":"hr-3-3","goals":["career"],"title":{"en":"Fair Evaluation","tr":"Adil Değerlendirme","fa":"ارزیابی منصفانه"},"cards":[{"word":"objective","sentence":"Keep your notes objective: facts and quotes only.","meaning":{"en":"Based on facts, not feelings.","tr":"nesnel.","fa":"عینی؛ بی‌طرفانه (بر پایه‌ی واقعیت، نه احساس)"}},{"word":"subjective","sentence":"\"Nice guy\" is a subjective comment.","meaning":{"en":"Based on personal feelings or taste.","tr":"öznel.","fa":"ذهنی؛ سلیقه‌ای (بر پایه‌ی احساس یا سلیقه‌ی شخصی)"}},{"word":"criteria","sentence":"We score every candidate against the same five criteria.","meaning":{"en":"The standards used to judge something (singular: criterion).","tr":"ölçütler, kriterler.","fa":"معیارها (مفرد: criterion)"}},{"word":"score","sentence":"Score each answer from 1 to 4 before you discuss it.","meaning":{"en":"To give a number to show how good something is.","tr":"puanlamak.","fa":"امتیاز دادن؛ نمره دادن"}},{"word":"justify","sentence":"Can you justify that score with an example?","meaning":{"en":"To give a good reason for something.","tr":"gerekçelendirmek.","fa":"دلیل موجه آوردن؛ توجیه کردن"}},{"word":"appear to","sentence":"He appears to work well under pressure.","gap":"appears to","accept":["appears to","appear to"],"meaning":{"en":"To seem to, from what you can see.","tr":"... gibi görünmek.","fa":"به نظر رسیدن (از روی آنچه می‌بینی)"}},{"word":"consistent","sentence":"Her answers were consistent with her CV.","meaning":{"en":"The same, or in agreement, each time.","tr":"tutarlı.","fa":"یکدست؛ ثابت (هر بار یکسان)"}},{"word":"gut feeling","sentence":"A gut feeling is not evidence.","meaning":{"en":"A strong feeling you cannot fully explain.","tr":"içgüdü, sezgi.","fa":"حس درونی؛ دل‌گواهی"}},{"word":"quote","sentence":"Write a short quote from the answer.","meaning":{"en":"The exact words someone said.","tr":"alıntı.","fa":"نقل قول (عین کلمات کسی)"}},{"word":"panel discussion","sentence":"We compare scores in the panel discussion.","meaning":{"en":"The talk where interviewers decide together.","tr":"heyet değerlendirme görüşmesi.","fa":"جلسه‌ی جمع‌بندی هیئت مصاحبه (جایی که با هم تصمیم می‌گیرند)"}}]},"story":{"id":"c-hr-3-3-s","level":"B1","genre":"Workplace","course":"hr","unit":"hr-3-3","title":{"en":"What She Said","tr":"Onun Söyledikleri","fa":"آنچه او گفت"},"text":"At six in the evening, Omar's interview notes arrived from Dubai. They were short.\n\n\"Karim: nice guy, a bit lazy maybe. Young, will want more money soon. Hana: good, but she has two kids, so night shifts could be a problem.\"\n\nLeyla read them twice. She had been in the same interviews, on the same screen. She remembered different things.\n\nShe opened her own notes. Karim had arrived on time. He said he had trained two new drivers in his last job. He told them he could start immediately. When she asked about night routes, he said he had never driven at night. Lazy? She could not find one word that showed it.\n\nHana said she had managed cold-chain deliveries for four years. She gave two examples with dates. Nobody had asked her about children, and nobody should have. Omar had seen a photo behind her on the video call.\n\nLeyla called him. \"Your notes are short,\" she said carefully. \"Mine are longer. Can I read you one line from each?\"\n\nShe read: \"Karim said he had trained two new drivers. There is limited evidence of night-shift experience.\" Then: \"Hana told us she had managed cold-chain deliveries for four years.\"\n\nOmar was silent. \"That's the same people,\" he said.\n\n\"It's the same people,\" Leyla said. \"But if Hana asks to see her notes one day, I would be happy for her to read mine.\"\n\nA long pause. Then Omar said, \"Delete the line about the kids.\" He did not say thank you. But the next morning his notes on the last candidate had three quotes in them.","vocab":[{"word":"carefully","en":"Here: in a careful, polite way, to avoid upsetting someone.","tr":"özenle, dikkatlice","fa":"با ملاحظه؛ با احتیاط و ادب (تا کسی نرنجد)"},{"word":"immediately","en":"At once, now.","tr":"hemen","fa":"فوراً؛ بی‌درنگ"},{"word":"silent","en":"Not speaking.","tr":"sessiz","fa":"ساکت"},{"word":"pause","en":"A short stop in speaking.","tr":"duraklama","fa":"مکث"},{"word":"delete","en":"To remove written text.","tr":"silmek","fa":"پاک کردن"}],"quiz":[{"prompt":"Why were Omar's notes a problem?","options":["They were in the wrong order","They had opinions and personal details instead of evidence","They were too long"],"correct":1},{"prompt":"Choose the correct note.","options":["Karim said us he had trained two drivers.","Karim told he had trained two drivers.","Karim told us he had trained two drivers."],"correct":2},{"prompt":"What changed in Omar's notes the next morning?","options":["They had quotes from the candidate","They were deleted","They were written by Leyla"],"correct":0},{"prompt":"How might Hana feel if she read Omar's first note?","options":["Pleased that he noticed her family","Judged on her family, not on her work","Sure that she got the job"],"correct":1}],"notice":{"en":"Omar and Leyla sat in the same interviews. Compare their notes: which words are facts, and which are guesses?","tr":"Omar ve Leyla aynı mülakatlardaydı. Notlarını karşılaştır: hangi kelimeler bilgi, hangileri tahmin?","fa":"عمر و لیلا در همان مصاحبه‌ها بودند. یادداشت‌هایشان را مقایسه کن: کدام کلمه‌ها واقعیت‌اند و کدام‌ها حدس؟"},"bridge":{"en":"'Karim said he had trained two new drivers.' Next: see how reported speech keeps notes fair.","tr":"'Karim said he had trained two new drivers.' Sırada: dolaylı anlatımın notları nasıl adil tuttuğunu gör.","fa":"«⁨Karim said he had trained two new drivers.⁩» قدم بعد: ببین نقل قول غیرمستقیم چطور یادداشت را منصفانه نگه می‌دارد."}},"speaking":{"id":"hr-3-3","course":"hr","unit":"hr-3-3","topic":{"en":"Reporting Back on a Candidate","tr":"Bir Aday Hakkında Geri Bildirim Sunmak","fa":"گزارش دادن درباره‌ی یک متقاضی"},"warmup":{"en":"Think of someone you judged quickly and later saw differently. What changed your mind?","tr":"Hızlıca yargıladığın ve sonra farklı gördüğün birini düşün. Fikrini ne değiştirdi?","fa":"کسی را به یاد بیاور که درباره‌اش زود قضاوت کردی و بعدها جور دیگری دیدیش. چه چیزی نظرت را عوض کرد؟"},"questions":[{"en":"Tell Omar three things the candidate said. Use said and told.","tr":"Omar'a adayın söylediği üç şeyi anlat. Said ve told kullan.","fa":"سه چیز را که متقاضی گفت برای عمر بازگو کن. از said و told استفاده کن."},{"en":"Give one evaluation with a hedge: seems, appears, or there is limited evidence of.","tr":"Bir yumuşatıcıyla bir değerlendirme yap: seems, appears ya da there is limited evidence of.","fa":"ارزیابی‌ات را با زبان محتاط بگو: seems، appears یا there is limited evidence of."},{"en":"Omar says: \"Just tell me if you liked him.\" Answer politely, with evidence.","tr":"Omar diyor ki: \"Sadece onu sevip sevmediğini söyle.\" Kibarca ve kanıtla cevap ver.","fa":"عمر می‌گوید: «⁨Just tell me if you liked him.⁩» مؤدبانه و با تکیه بر شواهد جواب بده."}],"followups":[{"en":"Give the whole report in 90 seconds, then 60, then 45.","tr":"Raporun tamamını 90, sonra 60, sonra 45 saniyede ver.","fa":"کل گزارش را یک بار در ۹۰ ثانیه، بعد در ۶۰ و بعد در ۴۵ ثانیه بگو."},{"en":"Now report one thing a colleague said to you today: he said, she told me.","tr":"Şimdi bugün bir iş arkadaşının sana söylediği bir şeyi aktar: he said, she told me.","fa":"حالا چیزی را که امروز همکارت به تو گفت نقل کن: he said، she told me."}],"expressions":[{"phrase":"He told us (that)...","meaning":{"en":"Reports a fact from the interview.","tr":"Mülakattan bir olguyu aktarır.","fa":"یک واقعیت از مصاحبه را گزارش می‌کند."}},{"phrase":"There is limited evidence of...","meaning":{"en":"Names a gap without judging the person.","tr":"Kişiyi yargılamadan bir eksikliği belirtir.","fa":"یک کمبود را می‌گوید، بدون قضاوت درباره‌ی خود شخص."}},{"phrase":"Based on what she said, ...","meaning":{"en":"Links your view to the evidence.","tr":"Görüşünü kanıta bağlar.","fa":"نظر تو را به شواهد گره می‌زند."}}],"culture":{"en":"Many international companies ask each panel member to score every answer alone before the panel discussion, so the most senior voice does not decide for everyone. In hierarchical workplaces, a junior interviewer may not want to disagree with a manager out loud; written scores first protect their view.","tr":"Birçok uluslararası şirket, heyetteki herkesin her cevabı değerlendirme toplantısından önce tek başına puanlamasını ister; böylece en kıdemli kişinin sesi herkes adına karar vermez. Hiyerarşik işyerlerinde daha az kıdemli bir görüşmeci bir yöneticiye yüksek sesle itiraz etmek istemeyebilir; önce yazılı puan vermek onun görüşünü korur.","fa":"بسیاری از شرکت‌های بین‌المللی از هر عضو هیئت مصاحبه می‌خواهند پیش از جلسه‌ی جمع‌بندی، به هر جواب جداگانه و تنهایی امتیاز بدهد، تا نظر ارشدترین فرد جای نظر همه را نگیرد. در محیط‌های کاری سلسله‌مراتبی، مصاحبه‌گرِ کم‌سابقه‌تر ممکن است نخواهد جلوی مدیر مخالفتش را بلند بگوید؛ امتیازی که از قبل نوشته شده، از نظر او محافظت می‌کند."},"model":"Omar, here is my report on Karim. He said he had driven for two years and held a Class C licence. He told us he had trained two new drivers in his last job, and he said he could start immediately. There is limited evidence of night-shift experience. Based on what he said, he appears to be a clear communicator, so I recommend him for a day route.","selfCheck":[{"en":"I reported three things with said and told correctly.","tr":"Üç şeyi said ve told'u doğru kullanarak aktardım.","fa":"سه چیز را با کاربرد درست said و told گزارش کردم."},{"en":"I moved the tense back (had driven, could start).","tr":"Zamanı geriye kaydırdım (had driven, could start).","fa":"زمان فعل را به عقب بردم (had driven، could start)."},{"en":"I gave one evaluation with a hedge.","tr":"Bir değerlendirmeyi yumuşatma ifadesiyle verdim.","fa":"یک ارزیابی را با زبانی محتاط گفتم."},{"en":"I used no labels about age, family or personality.","tr":"Yaş, aile ya da kişilik hakkında etiket kullanmadım.","fa":"هیچ برچسبی درباره‌ی سن، خانواده یا شخصیت به کار نبردم."}]},"judge":{"id":"c-hr-3-3-j","course":"hr","unit":"hr-3-3","type":"judge","parts":["Opinion","Personal detail","No evidence"],"instruction":{"en":"Tap the problems you find in each interview note. A good note has none.","tr":"Her mülakat notunda bulduğun sorunlara dokun. İyi bir notta hiç sorun yoktur.","fa":"در هر یادداشت مصاحبه، مشکل‌هایی را که می‌بینی لمس کن. یادداشت خوب هیچ مشکلی ندارد."},"items":[{"answer":"Karim: nice guy, a bit lazy maybe.","present":["Opinion","No evidence"],"fix":{"en":"Opinion words (\"nice\", \"lazy\") and no example. Write what he said or did: \"He arrived on time and answered all five questions.\"","tr":"Görüş bildiren sözcükler (\"nice\", \"lazy\") ve hiç örnek yok. Ne söylediğini ya da yaptığını yaz: \"He arrived on time and answered all five questions.\"","fa":"کلمه‌های نظری (nice، lazy) آمده و هیچ مثالی نیست. بنویس او چه گفت یا چه کرد: «⁨He arrived on time and answered all five questions.⁩»"}},{"answer":"Hana has two young children, so night shifts could be a problem.","present":["Personal detail","No evidence"],"fix":{"en":"Family is not a job criterion, and this is a guess. Ask every candidate the same question: \"This role includes night shifts. Is that possible for you?\"","tr":"Aile bir iş ölçütü değildir ve bu bir tahmindir. Her adaya aynı soruyu sor: \"This role includes night shifts. Is that possible for you?\"","fa":"خانواده معیار شغلی نیست و این فقط یک حدس است. از همه‌ی متقاضیان یک سؤال یکسان بپرس: «⁨This role includes night shifts. Is that possible for you?⁩»"}},{"answer":"Hana said she had managed cold-chain deliveries for four years and gave two dated examples.","present":[],"fix":null},{"answer":"Strong accent, might be hard for clients to understand.","present":["Personal detail","No evidence"],"fix":{"en":"An accent is not a criterion. If clear speech matters, note evidence: \"He explained the route clearly; I did not need to ask him to repeat.\"","tr":"Aksan bir ölçüt değildir. Açık konuşma önemliyse kanıt yaz: \"He explained the route clearly; I did not need to ask him to repeat.\"","fa":"لهجه معیار نیست. اگر واضح حرف زدن برای این شغل مهم است، شاهد بنویس: «⁨He explained the route clearly; I did not need to ask him to repeat.⁩»"}},{"answer":"Karim is young, so he will probably want more money soon.","present":["Personal detail","No evidence"],"fix":{"en":"Age is a personal detail and the money point is a guess. Note what he said: \"Expected salary: 8,000 dirhams.\"","tr":"Yaş kişisel bir bilgidir ve para konusu bir tahmindir. Söylediğini not et: \"Expected salary: 8,000 dirhams.\"","fa":"سن جزو اطلاعات شخصی است و حرف پول هم فقط یک حدس است. همان را بنویس که خودش گفت: «⁨Expected salary: 8,000 dirhams.⁩»"}}]},"writing":{"id":"c-hr-3-3-w","title":{"en":"Fair notes on Karim","tr":"Karim için adil notlar","fa":"یادداشت‌های منصفانه درباره‌ی کریم"},"course":"hr","unit":"hr-3-3","type":"writing","difficulty":"medium","prompt":{"en":"Rewrite Omar's notes on Karim as objective notes: 3-4 facts in reported speech, one hedged gap, then a recommendation of 1-2 sentences.","tr":"Omar'ın Karim hakkındaki notlarını nesnel notlar olarak yeniden yaz: aktarma cümleleriyle 3-4 olgu, yumuşatılmış bir eksik, ardından 1-2 cümlelik bir öneri.","fa":"یادداشت‌های عمر درباره‌ی کریم را به یادداشتی بی‌طرفانه تبدیل کن: سه یا چهار واقعیت با نقل قول غیرمستقیم، یک کمبود با زبان محتاط و در آخر یک توصیه‌ی یکی‌دو جمله‌ای."},"model":"Candidate: Karim Nasser. He said he had driven for two years and held a Class C licence. He told us he had trained two new drivers in his last job. He said he could start immediately. There is limited evidence of night-shift experience. Recommendation: Karim appears to be a clear communicator and he is available at once. However, he has less driving experience than the other candidates, so I recommend him for a day route.","frame":"Candidate: ___. He said he had ___. He told us he had ___. He said he could ___. There is limited evidence of ___. Recommendation: ___ appears to be ___. However, ___, so I recommend ___.","words":[{"word":"said"},{"word":"told"},{"word":"evidence"}],"minWords":60,"minSentences":6,"rubric":["Task done: 3-4 facts, one gap, a recommendation","Organised: facts first, then evaluation, then recommendation","Language: said / told + person; tense moved back; one hedge","Tone: objective; no opinions, age, family or accent"],"rubricI18n":{"tr":["Görev: 3-4 bilgi, bir eksik, bir öneri","Düzen: önce bilgiler, sonra değerlendirme, sonra öneri","Dil: said / told + kişi; zaman bir adım geri; bir yumuşatma ifadesi","Üslup: nesnel; yorum, yaş, aile ya da aksan yok"],"fa":["کامل بودن کار: سه یا چهار واقعیت، یک کمبود، یک پیشنهاد","نظم: اول واقعیت‌ها، بعد ارزیابی، بعد پیشنهاد","زبان: said و told با شخص؛ زمان فعل یک قدم به عقب؛ یک عبارت محتاطانه","لحن: عینی؛ بدون نظر شخصی و بدون اشاره به سن، خانواده یا لهجه"]},"portfolio":"hr-final-3","parts":[{"t":{"en":"Facts in reported speech","tr":"Aktarılan sözlerle bilgiler","fa":"اطلاعات به شکل نقل قول غیرمستقیم"},"find":["he said","he told","she said"],"sample":"he said he had driven for two years and held a Class C licence"},{"t":{"en":"One gap, stated calmly","tr":"Sakince belirtilen bir eksik","fa":"یک کمبود که آرام گفته شود"},"find":["limited evidence","no example","there is limited"],"sample":"limited evidence of night-shift work"},{"t":{"en":"A recommendation","tr":"Bir öneri","fa":"یک پیشنهاد"},"find":["recommend","recommendation"],"sample":"recommend him for a day route"}]},"perspective":{"id":"c-hr-3-3-p","title":{"en":"Karim reads his notes","tr":"Karim notlarını okuyor","fa":"کریم یادداشت‌هایش را می‌خواند"},"course":"hr","unit":"hr-3-3","type":"perspective","minSentences":2,"prompt":{"en":"You are Karim. Months later you ask to see your interview notes. Write 2-3 sentences in first person: which line feels fair, and which line would have hurt if it were still there?","tr":"Karim'sin. Aylar sonra mülakat notlarını görmek istiyorsun. Birinci tekil şahısla 2-3 cümle yaz: hangi satır adil geliyor ve hangi satır hâlâ orada olsaydı seni incitirdi?","fa":"تو کریم هستی. چند ماه بعد درخواست می‌کنی یادداشت‌های مصاحبه‌ات را ببینی. از زبان خودت دو یا سه جمله بنویس: کدام خط به نظرت منصفانه است، و اگر کدام خط هنوز آنجا بود، دلت را می‌شکست؟"}},"exit":{"id":"c-hr-3-3-x","course":"hr","unit":"hr-3-3","type":"exit","items":[{"from":"hr-3-3","kind":"blank","prompt":"He ___ that he had worked nights for two years.","options":["told","said","spoke"],"correct":1,"point":2,"why":{"en":"said: 'say' takes no person after it, so 'said that'. 'Told' needs a person (told us), and 'spoke' doesn't report words with that.","tr":"said: 'say' kendinden sonra kişi almaz, bu yüzden 'said that'. 'Told' bir kişi ister (told us); 'spoke' sözleri that ile aktarmaz.","fa":"said درست است، چون بعد از say شخص نمی‌آید: said that. told شخص می‌خواهد (told us) و spoke حرف را با that نقل نمی‌کند."},"hint2":{"en":"Look right after the gap: that comes straight after it, with no person in between. Which reporting verb works without a person?","tr":"Boşluğun hemen sağına bak: Arada kişi olmadan doğrudan that geliyor. Hangi aktarma fiili kişi olmadan kullanılır?","fa":"بلافاصله بعد از جای خالی را ببین: ⁨that⁩ بدون هیچ شخصی آمده. کدام فعلِ نقل قول بدون شخص به کار می‌رود؟"}},{"from":"hr-3-3","kind":"blank","prompt":"His answers give ___ evidence of night-shift experience.","options":["limited","few","many"],"correct":0,"point":2,"why":{"en":"limited: 'evidence' is uncountable, and 'limited evidence' is the careful way to say there is not much. 'Few' and 'many' go with countable plurals.","tr":"limited: 'evidence' sayılamaz; 'limited evidence' fazla kanıt olmadığını söylemenin dikkatli yoludur. 'Few' ve 'many' sayılabilen çoğullarla gelir.","fa":"limited درست است، چون evidence شمارش‌ناپذیر است و limited evidence شیوه‌ی محتاطانه‌ی گفتن «شاهد زیادی نیست» است. few و many با اسم جمعِ شمارش‌پذیر می‌آیند."}},{"from":"hr-3-3","kind":"mcq","prompt":"Which interview note is objective?","options":["She seemed nice.","She said she had led a team of four.","She is probably too young."],"correct":1,"point":1,"why":{"en":"'She said she had led a team of four' records what was said. 'Seemed nice' is a feeling, and 'too young' is a judgement you must not write.","tr":"'She said she had led a team of four' söyleneni kaydeder. 'Seemed nice' bir duygudur; 'too young' yazmaman gereken bir yargıdır.","fa":"«She said she had led a team of four» چیزی را ثبت می‌کند که گفته شد. seemed nice یک حس است و too young قضاوتی است که نباید بنویسی."}},{"from":"hr-3-2","kind":"blank","prompt":"Can you tell me what ___ next?","options":["did you do","you did","you do did"],"correct":1,"point":2,"why":{"en":"you did: inside 'Can you tell me what...', use statement order and no extra did. 'Did you do' is question order, and 'you do did' doubles the verb.","tr":"you did: 'Can you tell me what...' içinde düz sıra kullanılır, fazladan did gelmez. 'Did you do' soru sırasıdır; 'you do did' fiili iki kez kullanır.","fa":"you did درست است، چون بعد از Can you tell me what ترتیب خبری می‌آید و did اضافه لازم نیست. did you do ترتیب سؤالی است و you do did فعل را دوتایی می‌کند."},"hint2":{"en":"After Can you tell me, the question turns into a statement: subject, then verb. Which option has that order?","tr":"Can you tell me’dan sonra soru düz cümleye döner: önce özne, sonra fiil. Hangi seçenekte bu sıra var?","fa":"بعد از ⁨Can you tell me⁩، سؤال به جمله‌ی خبری تبدیل می‌شود: اول فاعل، بعد فعل. کدام گزینه این ترتیب را دارد؟"}},{"from":"hr-2-4","kind":"blank","prompt":"Neither candidate ___ cold-chain experience.","options":["have","has","having"],"correct":1,"point":2,"why":{"en":"has: 'neither candidate' is singular, so has. 'Have' is plural, and 'having' isn't a full verb.","tr":"has: 'neither candidate' tekildir, bu yüzden has. 'Have' çoğuldur; 'having' tam fiil değildir.","fa":"has درست است، چون neither candidate مفرد است. have جمع است و having فعل کامل نیست."}},{"from":"hr-1-3","kind":"blank","prompt":"Sorry, could you ___ your surname, please?","options":["spell","spelling","to spell"],"correct":0,"point":2,"why":{"en":"spell: 'could you' + plain verb. 'Spelling' and 'to spell' don't follow could.","tr":"spell: 'could you' + yalın fiil. 'Spelling' ve 'to spell' could'dan sonra gelmez.","fa":"spell درست است، چون بعد از could you فعل ساده می‌آید. spelling و to spell بعد از could نمی‌آیند."}}]}}; })(globalThis.COURSE_FILES = globalThis.COURSE_FILES || {});
